		{
			description: [
				"I still remember my steamwork classes. I am still able to make very simple steam machines."
				""
				"The Boiler is a simple piece of machinery. When provided with fuel, it will power nearby steam-powered machines."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"&o&7Notes from Eleonore's Travels, Tome II"
				""
				"&fThe boiler is most often used as a component piece in other machines, but it has its own uses, typically to power other low-tech equipment with steam, such as the steam-powered macerator or steam-powered tree feller."
			]
			entity_vis_size: 1.0f
			id: "3A5B721A7E614679"
			rewards: [
				{
					count: 32
					id: "20C133D9061BFEB7"
					item: "minecraft:coal"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "7272728BCA495D7F"
					type: "xp_levels"
					xp_levels: 1
				}
			]
			tasks: [{
				id: "2DC699AF1510ECA4"
				item: "concatenatedadditionsmachines:boiler"
				type: "item"
			}]
			x: -11.0d
			y: -7.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["3A5B721A7E614679"]
			description: [
				"When powered by a nearby boiler, it will cut down trees as they grow from saplings. It can do this from the front or the back with its sawblades. It's programmed to only cut down trees as they grow, not chop already existing trees."
				""
				"When a chest is placed above it, its inventory will be poured in there. When provided with bone meal and saplings, it can replant trees automatically, but only at the front."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"&o&7Notes from Eleonore's Travels, Tome II"
				""
				"&fThe Steam-Powered Tree Feller is a great low-tech automation machine to take care of trees. It requires an adjacent active boiler to work. It is then able to fell entire trees with either its front or back sawblades. If a chest is placed on top of the tree feller, then the contents will be deposited in there."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"&fIt can also accommodate storage for saplings and bone meal to grow trees autonomously. One bone meal is consumed per sapling planted, and it does not use the bone meal on the sapling to grow it faster automatically. Saplings are replanted on the felling of trees."
			]
			entity_vis_size: 1.0f
			id: "5DC0FCAE66BF00E8"
			rewards: [
				{
					count: 48
					id: "2C1AE4AD9F8D305F"
					item: "minecraft:coal"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "7FC30420BC8DAB74"
					type: "xp_levels"
					xp_levels: 1
				}
			]
			tasks: [{
				id: "4C6591E3F784116A"
				item: "concatenatedadditionsmachines:hydraulic_tree_feller"
				type: "item"
			}]
			x: -11.5d
			y: -8.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["3A5B721A7E614679"]
			description: [
				"When powered by a nearby boiler, it will crush ingots into powder. These powders can be useful for alloying but also for ore processing."
				""
				"It is more efficient to crush raw ore into powder rather than fully formed ingots, which then can be smelted into multiple nuggets. This way, more ore can be extracted than in traditional smelting. I calculate this can make up to 1.77x ore processing."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"&o&7Notes from Eleonore's Travels, Tome II"
				""
				"&fThe Steam-Powered Crusher is a low-tech machine capable of crushing metals into not quite dust or fine powder, but something close enough. "
				""
				"&f[...] The most commonly crushed metals with this machine are, of course, iron and zinc, but also metals harder to crush with your bare hands and a hammer: copper and tin. &mThis can be used to make bronze.&r"
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"&fTo be powered, the crusher requires a nearby boiler within a one-block radius. The boiler must be active, thus requiring water and fuel inside. Water can be inserted with a bucket &a(right-click the boiler with it)&r."
			]
			entity_vis_size: 1.0f
			id: "00A7C3C7A6E8A59D"
			rewards: [
				{
					id: "0F344F06BB470BFD"
					item: "minecraft:water_bucket"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "736FB4B3D6DBB1F7"
					type: "xp_levels"
					xp_levels: 1
				}
			]
			tasks: [{
				id: "296FF6FE0366906B"
				item: "concatenatedadditionsmachines:hydraulic_crusher"
				type: "item"
			}]
			x: -13.0d
			y: -7.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["3A5B721A7E614679"]
			description: [
				"Hmm, I'm not quite sure of what meteorite can do.."
				""
				"&4Fine, I'll regurgitate some of the knowledge I have on the matter."
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"&o&7Notes from Eleonore's Travels, Tome I"
				""
				"&fPanvita is a universal plant able to be grafted to any other plant and adapt to its host. This is most often used by holders of the &m-------- ----&r&f to grow more oreberry bushes, which do not reproduce naturally, requiring panvita to be grafted to them. "
				""
				"&f&lPanvita exclusively grows via the Incubator.&r"
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"&fThe Incubator needs to be filled with water to start the growing process. You can use a water bucket for this purpose. Panvita will start to grow with a minimum of 100mb of water and will consume 80mb on growth."
				""
				"&fYou will have to wait in all likelihood for a few days for a single panvita to grow, although it may take less time."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"&fPanvita can be grafted to a wide variety of plants, flowers, and mushrooms, or can be turned into bonemeal."
				""
				"&fWhile oreberry bushes can only be planted in the dark, essence berry bushes can also be planted in the light."
			]
			entity_vis_size: 1.0f
			icon: "concatenatedadditionsmachines:berry_incubator"
			id: "6C22CAEF1156612C"
			rewards: [
				{
					id: "64B18EAC5D7F6FA6"
					item: "oreberriesreplanted:iron_oreberry_bush"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
